# E2E Cucumber Conventions

## Feature Files — Business Activities Only (ADR 0002)

See [`docs/adr/0002-declarative-feature-files.md`](../../docs/adr/0002-declarative-feature-files.md) for the full decision record.

**Feature files must express business activities and outcomes only.** UI interactions, button names, form field details, and technical setup are hidden inside step definitions and page objects.

### Rules

- Steps describe what the user *does in business terms*, not how the UI is operated.
- Business data (rates, amounts, counts) belongs in the feature file; test fixture details do not.
- Assertions express business outcomes, not UI state (e.g. "modal closes").
- Use a DataTable when verifying multiple related business values at once.

```gherkin
# ✅ Business-focused — correct
Feature: Add Income
    As a registered individual user
    I want to add my income for the month
    So that I can get paid

    @add-income
    Scenario: Individual user submits monthly income
        Given I am an individual user with daily income rate of 500 baht per day
        When I submit income for 18 work days and 20 hours of special work at 100 baht per hour
        Then the income confirmation breakdown should be:
            | net daily income   | 9000  |
            | net special income | 2000  |
            | net income         | 10670 |
        When I confirm the income submission
        Then my net income on the dashboard should be 10670 baht
```

```gherkin
# ❌ UI-focused — wrong
When I click the Add Income button
And I fill in special income "100" and working hours "20"
And I fill in work date "18"
And I click the Submit button
```

## Page Object Pattern (ADR 0001)

See [`docs/adr/0001-page-object-pattern.md`](../../docs/adr/0001-page-object-pattern.md) for the full decision record.

**All Playwright selectors and interactions must live in page object classes under `e2e/cucumber/pages/`.** Step definitions contain no selectors — only page object method calls and assertions.

### File structure

```
e2e/cucumber/
  features/
    <feature>.feature   ← business scenarios only
  pages/
    <name>.page.ts      ← selectors and interactions live here
  steps/
    <name>.steps.ts     ← page object calls + assertions only
  fixtures/
    test-idcard.pdf     ← test assets
```

### Page object contract

- Constructor receives a Playwright `Page` instance
- One `Page` instance shared across all page objects in `Before` hook
- Methods named after user actions or observable state, not selectors

```typescript
// pages/add-income-modal.page.ts
export class AddIncomeModalPage {
  constructor(private page: Page) {}

  async clickAddIncomeButton() {
    await this.page.locator("#btn-add").click();
  }

  async getConfirmationAmount(selector: string): Promise<number> {
    const text = await this.page.locator(selector).textContent() ?? "";
    return parseFloat(text.replace(/[^0-9.]/g, ""));
  }
}

// steps/login.steps.ts  ✅ correct — page object call only
When("I submit income for ...", async function (...) {
  await addIncomeModalPage.clickAddIncomeButton();
  // ...
});

// steps/login.steps.ts  ❌ wrong — selector in step file
When("I submit income for ...", async function (...) {
  await page.locator("#btn-add").click();
});
```

## Step Definitions (`e2e/cucumber/steps/*.steps.ts`)

- Use `chromium` via Playwright; instantiate all page objects in the `Before` hook
- `APP_URL` is `http://localhost:4200`
- Keycloak runs at `localhost:9000`; credentials are `e2e` / `s3cr3t`
- MongoDB connection: `mongodb://admin:admin@127.0.0.1:27017/odds_worklog_db?authSource=admin`
- For file upload steps, reference fixtures from `e2e/cucumber/fixtures/`

### Test data setup and cleanup

Use MongoDB directly in `Before`/`After` hooks to set up preconditions and clean up after tagged scenarios:

```typescript
After({ tags: "@add-income" }, async function () {
  if (addIncomeUserId) {
    await clearUserIncome(addIncomeUserId);
    await clearUserRegistration(addIncomeUserId);
  }
});
```

### DataTable steps

Use Cucumber's `DataTable` with `table.rowsHash()` for two-column key-value tables:

```typescript
import { DataTable } from "@cucumber/cucumber";

Then("the income confirmation breakdown should be:", async function (table: DataTable) {
  for (const [label, value] of Object.entries(table.rowsHash())) {
    const displayed = await addIncomeModalPage.getConfirmationAmount(SELECTORS[label]);
    assert.strictEqual(displayed, parseFloat(value), `${label}: expected ${value}`);
  }
});
```

## Running Tests

### Prerequisites

Start the following services before running E2E tests (each in its own terminal):

```bash
# 1. Start Docker infrastructure (MongoDB + Keycloak) — in api.odds-worklog/
make up

# 2. Start API server (port 8080) — in api.odds-worklog/
make run

# 3. Start Angular dev server (port 4200) — in web.odds-worklog/
make run
```

### Run E2E

```bash
make e2e                        # run all scenarios
make e2e ARGS="--tags @tag"     # run tagged scenarios only
```
